.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-BOUNCE-TLS-SERVICES 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-bounce-tls-services
.Nd make the services that serve the console's certificate load a new one
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A service reads its TLS certificate when it starts.
After
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8
writes a new one,
.Nm
makes each service that holds the old one pick up the new:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Xr nginx 8
is reloaded, so open connections \(em terminals, live dashboards \(em are
not dropped;
.It
the console's older proxy, the web console, its terminal
.Pq Ql ttyd-k9s
and Grafana are restarted, those that are running.
.El
.Pp
It does nothing when the certificate is the one it last acted on, which it
knows by its SHA-256 digest; or while an install or a klab run is in
progress, since restarting the web console then kills the install it is
running.
Each restart is queued, not waited for.
.Pp
It first sets the certificate to mode 0644 and the key to 0640.
.Pp
.Pa kldload-tls-cert.service
runs it after each run of the certificate tool.
It needs root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description at the top of the script and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/tls/webui.crt , Pa webui.key
The certificate and key.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/tls/.bounced-sha256
The digest of the certificate last acted on.
.It Pa /var/run/kldload/installer-busy , Pa /var/run/klab/current-run.env
Present while an install or a klab run is in progress.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0; 2 for any argument other than
.Fl -help .
A reload or restart that fails is not reported.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, whose certificate had not
changed.
It writes only to the journal, read here from a cursor taken just before:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# cur=$(journalctl -n 0 --show-cursor -q | sed -n 's/^-- cursor: //p')
# kldload-bounce-tls-services
# (exited 0)
# journalctl --after-cursor "$cur" -t kldload-bounce-tls-services -o cat --no-pager
cert unchanged — nothing to restart
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr journalctl 1 ,
.Xr systemctl 1 ,
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8 ,
.Xr nginx 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-09-05 it restarted everything whenever it ran, and it runs on
every network change: a desktop saw 115 runs in a day, and the web console
and Grafana hit systemd's start limit and stopped.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Fl -help
ran it.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The chmod loosens the key that
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8
writes 0600; only the directory's mode, 0700, keeps other users out.
What it was for is not known.
.Pp
Failures to reload or restart are discarded.
